infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One component, many elements — two cost profiles
  desc as pays in the type system; asChild pays in the element tree
  compares
    - label as prop
      children
        - label Runtime cost near zero
          desc One read: const Comp = as ?? 'div'; types are erased
        - label Expensive in the types
          desc Conditional and mapped types over E extends ElementType
        - label Scales with call sites
          desc 4,000 Box sites added about 30s of tsc time
        - label Polymorphic ref per element
          desc Ref type re-derived at every call site
        - label Home: style primitives
          desc Box, Text, Stack — few own props, no behavior
    - label asChild and Slot
      children
        - label Types stay simple
          desc Each side keeps its own props; no type explosion
        - label Pays at runtime
          desc Slot clones the one child and merges the prop sets
        - label Merge rules to debug
          desc className concat, style child-wins, handlers child-first
        - label Throws on multiple children
          desc Children.only — and silent if the child drops props
        - label Home: behavior wrappers
          desc Button, every Trigger — behaviors stack on one element
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
